msgstr "La grafia della giuria"

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:61 77e1aa1848034f06b04d4be90db12b5b
msgid "Three separators, everywhere (``core/parse.py``):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:69 9a3af7c5a62446f8a70b6ab1b55b1484
msgid ""
"Errors raise ``ParseError`` rather than blanking the page. Whatever is typed"
" is checked inline by ``core.checks.bib_line``, which produces the ``?7`` / "
"``!3`` / ``-2`` / ``<4`` flags — one implementation, so one notation holds "
"in every field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:76 3ef0e4e832404133b8dd07b946ff4141
msgid "Bunch races"
msgstr "Prove di gruppo"

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:78 ab8918118af24cf2bbbb5a488606e738
msgid "points race / madison"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:79 a9dce8905c0f4a34adf43010ea832887
msgid ""
"5-3-2-1 to the first four of each sprint, 10-6-4-2 in the final sprint. A "
"lap gained is +20, a lap lost −20. Ties broken by the placing in the last "
"sprint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:83 b135bc8b814a445ba6fd823465f59718
msgid "tempo race"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:84 ac4b178bcee340688e31e3e3dd5691d4
msgid "1 point to the winner of each sprint. The ±20 lap rule applies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:86 cddfded9c0c14d2dbd3af8ae4c064a63
msgid "scratch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:87 20de7ca6bfcc4517864ae74c46dd1998
msgid "No points: the finishing order is the classification."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:90 a1add5a8368f4a76bbd991ad0c541ce3
msgid ""
"Riders are entered in the order they are eliminated; the first one out is "
"last, the winner is the last number typed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:93 e142fb598f34411d999fd6bd1eaa6b45
msgid ""
"A ``DNF`` keeps the points it scored; an ``ABD`` does not. Riders still in "
"an elimination print with a **blank position**, so the same sheet works as a"
" live provisional. A rider is never placed by the app for not having been "
"typed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:99 16fdffde3c094e438f1162a78a51f382
msgid "Timed races"
msgstr "Prove a cronometro"

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:101 13978739c08048b0ac8c8cbddd71a962
msgid ""
"Entrants are individual riders or whole teams, and a team has **one** time —"
" not a time typed on an arbitrary rider row."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:104 e6f45d97b0004edeb679a3358df249d1
msgid ""
"Finals are loaded from qualifying: the first four qualified ride two finals,"
" 3rd against 4th first and 1st against 2nd last. Each final assigns the "
"places it rides for; whoever did not qualify keeps the order — and the time "
"— of qualifying. A final that is not ridden is closed from the sidebar, "
"either as a dead heat (the two share the lower place, no champion named, no "
"time) or on the qualifying times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:111 8061c47c745b433fa1ed0b7aaf278588
msgid ""
"**Two at a time or one at a time** is a jury choice on *this* event, saved "
"with it: pursuits normally run two per heat, but a category may be sent off "
"one at a time like a team sprint. The sheets follow, counting starts instead"
" of heats."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:117 340a5d8ba72d45b4b58d7d06926dbbdc
msgid "Sprint"
msgstr "Velocità"

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:119 a99d983cc1b14e0c855f94654cc0c2a2
msgid "Composition follows the UCI tables in Part 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:121 2c8136edfd4845c5b77827656e427d5a
msgid ""
"Heats are seeded **serpentine** on the current ranking. With two riders per "
"heat that is the familiar mirror pairing ``N1-N24, N2-N23, …``; with seven "
"it reproduces the keirin table ``A: R1 R8 R9 R16 R17 R24 R25``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:124 9a28f92ddafa4aa580d62bb622093c22
msgid ""
"The riders who do not qualify go to the repechages, composed the same way "
"over the losers in order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:126 dcbf2fd893a7460481e57cb7c182f4c5
msgid ""
"Riders knocked out in a round rank below those knocked out later, and among "
"themselves by the 200 m qualifying time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:129 c88586d315a34b05ac3dad1e23e5dfe5
msgid ""
"Two schemes ship, picked on the 200 m: ``12`` (the default — 12 qualify, "
"four rounds, with repechages) and ``8`` (8 qualify, three rounds, none). "
"Nothing is hard-coded to a bracket: the number of heats and how many advance"
" come from the programme, so a category with fewer entries runs a shorter "
"bracket without a code change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:137 614c9066cb7c475ab57b9a6bc1bea744
msgid "Keirin"
msgstr "Keirin"

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:139 cf7d316b75b64b849268827845bf6842
msgid ""
"A keirin is not seeded off a qualifying race: there is no time to rank "
"anybody on, so the jury composes the first round itself. What the app "
"supplies is the **shape** of the tournament, from the number of entries, off"
" UCI table 3.2.135."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:143 0285f0b6d5884db7ac746e212356a02a
msgid "Two matrices do the composing, and neither is guessed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:145 111c7ed5c7f64d37b0b1049398e880f6
msgid ""
"the **repechages** take the riders each heat did not qualify and spread them"
" so that as few as possible meet again — firsts left behind in heat order, "
"seconds backwards, thirds backwards from one place further round. With four "
"heats of seven that reproduces the UCI 28-rider table line for line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:149 0ea26040a6844b4fb3746c28dc3340c2
msgid ""
"the **round that follows** deals the qualifiers one *place* at a time — all "
"the winners, then all the seconds, then the repêchés — snaking each block "
"and turning it round between blocks, so a heat winner and the rider it beat "
"do not line up together again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:156 1aadd0ff8afc4c9caa42e7eb77d8aa19
msgid "Omnium"
msgstr "Omnium"

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:158 563c307bc3a34b5785b6a47cdee68c5c
msgid ""
"Four races, one classification: **scratch, tempo race, elimination, points "
"race**, in that order."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:163 06b3ec6cfa154d4fb38ed42080d96859
msgid ""
"The four keys those races are scheduled under in ``programme.yaml`` and "
"saved under in ``races/<id>.json`` are programme vocabulary, not labels. "
"Translating them would stop the app finding a race. What the jury *reads* "
"comes from ``core.i18n``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:168 cdd132169b354366833c3883dbafbc03
msgid ""
"The first three are scored on the UCI placing scale — **40 for the win, then"
" −2 per place down to 2 for 20th, 1 from 21st on**. The points race is "
"different: the points actually scored in it are **added** to the running "
"total, so the standings can still be overturned in the last race."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:173 2c92020a48f240128fa2a893c6d6f0b4
msgid ""
"Ties are broken by the passage at the last sprint of the points race; where "
"that race has not been ridden, by the placing in the last race ridden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:176 baa7624a503b465b98e5504ffdb8217d
msgid ""
"An omnium's partial standings *are* the next race's start order, which is "
"why a rider taking ``DNS`` / ``DNF`` / ``ABD`` / ``DSQ`` in one race drops "
"out of every later partial and out of the final classification. They stay on"
" the sheet of the race where the status was written, which is where the "
"decision is published."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:184 e785cbe7516b4b9facf1edd7b77189d0
msgid "Derny"
msgstr "Derny"

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:186 ae84b73a74ea4a6dbb9b0db9d038c7f9
msgid "Called, not written up. The only thing stored is the call itself:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:192 65c6dcf8c8fa42979a65d5e058b8a44c
msgid ""
"The lap chart, who has lost a lap, the standings, the lap times and the "
"outliers are all derived from that list, every time it is drawn. Nothing is "
"cached and nothing is written twice, so a number typed by mistake is undone "
"by dropping its line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:197 06801be62bf947fcb081c9981981f3bc
msgid ""
"**How the laps are cut.** The head makes the lap: a new column opens the "
"moment a number is called that has already been called in the column now "
"open. It needs no button pressed at the right instant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:201 bc8bfdd24bc3492eb6bee09939e44b29
msgid ""
"**How a lap is lost.** A lapped rider does not pass in the column where the "
"leader passed twice — the number simply is not in it — and shows up again in"
" the column after. So a bib missing from the columns between two of its own "
"passages lost a lap there: the chart prints it back in grey where it should "
"have been and marks the reappearance in red."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:207 2e41ea67b51c4b79b7721d6f2e356997
msgid ""
"``?`` is the passage nobody read: it fills its place in the chart, never "
"cuts a lap (two ``?`` in one column are two different riders), is nobody's "
"lap and is in no classification, until the jury turns it into a bib."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:211 d468382d16aa494db5be929cbe97ed61
msgid ""
"Outliers: from the third lap time onward, mean and σ per rider; a lap "
"outside the jury's threshold (default 3σ) is flagged on the chart and on the"
" passage table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:217 8cec614b8654465fa739ada3439d8f01
msgid "Composed rounds (``kind: setup``)"
msgstr "Fasi composte (``kind: setup``)"

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:219 b965eb264fb94807b808f15ed355502b
msgid ""
"A madison and an omnium ridden in qualifying heats are composed by the jury,"
" not by a result. The programme declares a round with ``kind: setup`` — pair"
" composition for a madison (which also holds the pair numbers), heat "
"composition for an omnium — with ``eliminate: N`` on it. It is not on any "
"day and it produces no communiqué. The load control then deals the "
"qualifiers across what follows — in an omnium, across all four races, "
"interleaved by heat: 1st of heat 1, 1st of heat 2, 2nd of heat 1, …"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:229 cfe1c06234a144d39d965c0562d130c5
msgid "What a round files"
msgstr "Che cosa produce una fase"

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:231 4807d2b958e6448cb6a917a94788e37a
msgid ""
"``core.rounds`` proposes, for each round of a format: its distance, its laps"
" (from the track length), its sprints, how many qualify, how many are "
"eliminated (UCI 3.2.157), and the documents it may file (``docs_for``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference/formats.rst:235 a4757d48835940fc824bbd26e83c9f13
msgid ""
"Everything it returns is a **proposal**. ``propose_round`` re-proposes one "
"round, which is what the ↩ control on the Programme page restores; a value "
"that differs from the proposal is simply a value the jury chose. What it "
"cannot know it leaves empty — a keirin states its laps and no distance, "
"because no table here says how long a keirin is."
msgstr ""
